# Tauri regenerates these on every build and writes them with LF endings. This
# repository is used with `core.autocrlf=true`, so git otherwise expects CRLF in
# the worktree and reports both files as modified after every single build --
# with an empty diff, because the content is identical and only the endings
# differ. The cost is not cosmetic: `git status` never returns to clean, so it
# stops being a signal, and a real change sitting alongside them is easy to miss.
# They were discarded by hand five times in one session before this was written.
#
# Declaring them LF makes the worktree form match what the generator writes, so
# they stay clean until their content actually changes. Scoped to these generated
# files on purpose -- hand-written sources keep the repository's existing
# behaviour.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/schemas/*.json text eol=lf
